><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251023104525+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251023104533+10'00'" name="ef4f9568-e099-478e-af01-d71a94f4bfb7" page="1" coords="38.153500,427.389000,289.293000,427.389000,38.153500,417.434000,289.293000,417.593000,44.729700,416.957000,253.253000,416.957000,44.729700,407.162000,253.253000,407.162000,38.153500,406.469000,289.258000,406.469000,38.153500,396.515000,289.258000,396.674000,44.729700,396.038000,289.153000,396.038000,44.729700,386.243000,289.153000,386.243000,165.600000,386.518000,169.019000,386.518000,165.600000,379.988000,169.019000,379.988000,44.729700,385.550000,165.666000,385.550000,44.729700,375.755000,165.666000,375.755000,38.154300,375.116000,289.192000,375.116000,38.154300,365.161000,289.192000,365.321000,44.730500,364.628000,289.160000,364.628000,44.730500,354.833000,289.160000,354.833000,44.730500,354.197000,116.626000,354.197000,44.730500,344.401000,116.626000,344.401000,38.154300,343.709000,289.141000,343.709000,38.154300,333.754000,289.141000,333.913000,44.844500,333.277000,136.561000,333.277000,44.844500,323.482000,136.561000,323.482000" rect="37.847400,323.176000,289.599000,427.695000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>• We propose a pipeline for 3D motion capturewith regular video cameras&#xD;applicable to a wide range of recording environments.&#xD;• We introduce ASPset-510, a novel 3D pose dataset recorded in an outdoor&#xD;environmentwith awide variety of dynamic motion. ASPset-510&#xD;is publicly available for download.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-7.3pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>1&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>• We demonstrate that ASPset-510 training data is able to improve the&#xD;accuracy of 3D human pose estimation models by evaluating on an&#xD;existing benchmark.&#xD;• We present baseline evaluation results for ASPset-510 as a point of&#xD;reference for future work.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="1" rect="595.276000,335.389000,779.276000,427.389000"
/></highlight
